   Exemptions: neutral descriptions of the social context of the time, made without value judgments, for the purpose of explaining the causes of events in objective historical research; rigorous historical analysis that differentiates causes of death but still concludes it was systematic mass killing; background introductions that emphasize historical complexity without diminishing the nature of the crimes.

